  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "note",
   "x": -380,
   "y": 20,
   "on": true,
   "name": "",
   "params": {
    "text": "VIRTUAL PATCH RIG. Seven cells, one of each type, each alone in its own dish with an electrode in it. The current ramps from zero to 12 over the first three seconds and then holds, so the rate over time of each probe, read over those seconds, is that cell's current to rate curve, read left to right.",
    "width": 340,
    "near": ""
   },
   "inputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "note",
   "x": -380,
   "y": 200,
   "on": true,
   "name": "",
   "params": {
    "text": "TRY THIS: click a cell in the viewer to see its membrane potential. The current where a cell starts firing is its rheobase: TC and LTS start almost at once, RS needs about 4, FS about the same but fires far faster once it goes. RZ, a resonator, fires only in a narrow band. Change the ramp's current to see how far each curve goes.",
    "width": 340,
    "near": "the electrode"
   },
   "inputs": []
